menu.tip = From choosing the contest to submission and HAMLOG export
progress = {0} of {1} steps done
done = Done
step.1 = Choose the contest
step.1.text = In the zLog menu, choose the contest and create or open a log file. Closing the log returns to the zLog menu.
step.2 = Your station
step.2.text = Set your callsign, location and power per band in Options > Station. They make your sent number and the submission papers.
step.3 = Logging
step.3.text = Type the callsign, Space to the number, Enter to log, Esc to clear. F1 to F12 send the messages set in Options > CW keyer (phone: Options > Voice memory); the guide beside the entry row shows which key to press next. To send messages with Enter, turn on "Enter sends messages" in Options > Entry row. The call history fills in numbers from earlier logs.
step.4 = Check the score and dupes
step.4.text = The score is QSO points times multipliers. A multiplier is each new area worked on a band (prefecture, city, country, or as the contest rules say); the Multipliers window lists what is still missing. A dupe (second QSO with the same station on a band) scores nothing. The This station window shows what was worked, by band.
step.5 = Submit the log
step.5.text = Fill in the summary sheet in the submission window and save the JARL E-Log. R2.1 can be submitted on the JARL Web form.
step.6 = Export for HAMLOG
step.6.text = Export in the HAMLOG format (File > Export) to take QSOs into HAMLOG, also for QSL cards.
